<p>By locking all four wheels of the cargo area, we prevent any unauthorized access and, more importantly, stop the boxes from shifting due to sudden braking or turns. This stability is crucial for preventing inter-box collisions, which are a primary cause of packaging damage and subsequent scratches on the items inside.</p><h3>Edge Padding for Final Protection</h3><p>Finally, edge padding is applied to the corners and edges of furniture and crates. This high-density foam acts as a shock absorber, protecting the most vulnerable parts of your belongings from minor bumps during loading and unloading. Together, these protocols—joint inspection, hydraulic ramp loading, 4-wheel lock, and edge padding—form a robust safety net.</p>
